From 136e614f365c855c3897e4a96ac3b2bdede9feda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 03:00:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom_iommu: Guard optional global address calculation

Legacy instances have no per-instance configuration or global base. The
halt helpers currently add the micro-MMU offset to the NULL global base
before checking whether the helper is needed. An ASan/UBSan host fixture
executing the extracted production helper reports a nonzero offset from
a null pointer on that legacy path.

Derive the register address only after the configuration and halt guards
in both helpers. Keep the programmed path and all MMIO operations
intact. This addresses the imported integration feature; it is not a
claim that the new feature already exists in the current upstream IOMMU
base.

Fixes: 5ec3d506e602 ("iommu: qcom_iommu: halt the micro-MMU while programming context banks")

Prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance. Human review and DCO
certification remain pending. Host memory emulation does not qualify
hardware operation.

Backport this exact delta to the maintained 6.18.63 Fx0 tree. The
fork already carries the optional-global/halt implementation through
its checksum-pinned reconstructed r50 source overlay. The Fixes tag
identifies the original imported feature, not an upstream LTS commit.
The LTS extracted helpers pass four cases. Both original helpers are
byte-equal to the saved baseline and trigger the expected UBSan null
offset reports. These are UB reproducers, not clean behavioral controls.
No kernel ABI or physical behavior is established by the host model.

The combined LTS series compiles six selected MDP5, IOMMU and input
objects per profile: ARM normal, ARM64 normal and ARM64 RT. All three
verify nonpermissive CFI, with W=1 and no diagnostics. ARM32 RT is
unsupported by this LTS and is not counted. These object checks do
not qualify a full link, package update or hardware operation.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Human review and
DCO remain pending. No publication or maintainer contact is authorized.

Backported from commit d8c6a90c3b52480eeadd2dd4ceff95c0b46d4d9a
("iommu: qcom_iommu: Guard optional global address calculation")
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 7c42fb259aa2..541e79dd8a8b 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -387,12 +387,14 @@ static int qcom_iommu_reset_ns(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu)
  */
 static void qcom_iommu_halt(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu)
 {
-	void __iomem *reg = qcom_iommu->global_base + QCOM_IOMMU_MICRO_MMU_CTRL;
+	void __iomem *reg;
 	u32 val;
 
 	if (!qcom_iommu->cfg || !qcom_iommu->cfg->halt)
 		return;
 
+	reg = qcom_iommu->global_base + QCOM_IOMMU_MICRO_MMU_CTRL;
+
 	writel_relaxed(readl_relaxed(reg) | MICRO_MMU_CTRL_HALT_REQ, reg);
 
 	if (readl_poll_timeout(reg, val, val & MICRO_MMU_CTRL_IDLE, 0, 100000))
@@ -401,11 +403,13 @@ static void qcom_iommu_halt(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu)
 
 static void qcom_iommu_unhalt(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu)
 {
-	void __iomem *reg = qcom_iommu->global_base + QCOM_IOMMU_MICRO_MMU_CTRL;
+	void __iomem *reg;
 
 	if (!qcom_iommu->cfg || !qcom_iommu->cfg->halt)
 		return;
 
+	reg = qcom_iommu->global_base + QCOM_IOMMU_MICRO_MMU_CTRL;
+
 	writel_relaxed(readl_relaxed(reg) & ~MICRO_MMU_CTRL_HALT_REQ, reg);
 }
 
